From 69f357fec81759cec5a57d1a1d934ab5445654f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:03:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Integration of a batch for the behaviours generated by
 generic-parallel

- integrate(BatchExecutionPolicy, MaterialDataManager, options, dt[, b, e])
  integrates the points of a material data manager as a batch. The fields
  of the batch refer to the arrays of the manager, the material properties
  and the external state variables being given variable by variable
  (uniform values or values stored point by point): no data is copied.
  Invalid arguments and errors of the backend are reported by exceptions,
  never as failures of the integration. In case of failure, the index of
  the first point where the integration failed is reported.
- The integration functions of a material data manager switch to the
  integration of a batch for those behaviours, with the execution policy
  of the manager (batch_execution_policy). integrate_debug is refused.
- The uniform values stored by the manager are in the memory of the host:
  they are refused for the cuda and hip backends, which must be given
  spans on memory accessible by the device.
- The libraries are never unloaded (RTLD_NODELETE): the threads of TBB,
  used by the parallel algorithms of the C++ standard library, were still
  alive when the libraries were closed at the end of the process
  (intermittent crash at exit).

GenericParallelIntegrateTest compares the integration of batches with the
integration point by point of the generic interface (Norton over several
time steps, plasticity with the temperature given point by point, elastic
behaviour with material properties given point by point and uniform,
ranges of points, prediction, failure at all points).
